---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, site, power, network, publicDeployment as deployment } from '../data/site';
---
<Content
  title={`Colocation and dedicated compute in Mead | ${company.full}`}
  description={`Plan customer-owned hosting or dedicated B300 compute at ${site.designation}. Buildings A and C provide ${site.dataCenterArea.toLocaleString()} gross sq ft for data-center development.`}
  kicker="Colocation and dedicated compute"
  heading="Your hardware. Our campus."
  lede={`Develop your next deployment with SmartTec in ${site.name}. Buildings A and C provide ${site.dataCenterArea.toLocaleString()} gross sq ft for data-center development. Each customer allocation requires confirmed power, a complete cooling design and commissioning.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Data-center buildings', value: `${site.dataCenterArea.toLocaleString()} sq ft`, note: 'Buildings A and C, gross area' },
    { label: 'Utility', value: power.utility, note: power.service, tone: 'gold' },
    { label: 'Network plan', value: network.service, note: network.provider },
    { label: 'Current stage', value: 'Development', note: 'Fit-out and commissioning ahead', tone: 'signal' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="two-ways" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Choose your approach</span></p>
    <h2 id="two-ways">Bring your equipment or use our planned nodes.</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card__tag mono-label">Customer-owned hardware</p>
        <h3>Colocation</h3>
        <p>Keep ownership of your servers and software stack. We assess the space, power, cooling and connectivity needed for your equipment in Buildings A and C.</p>
        <p>Share rack dimensions, equipment weight, IT load and cooling requirements so we can develop an appropriate deployment proposal.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card__tag mono-label">SmartTec hardware</p>
        <h3>Dedicated compute</h3>
        <p>The initial proposal is {deployment.gpus} B300 GPUs in {deployment.systems} complete Supermicro systems, together in one building. Dedicated allocations remain subject to customer commitments, procurement, commissioning and an agreed offer.</p>
        <p><a href="/compute">Explore the B300 proposal →</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="infrastructure" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The campus</span></p>
    <h2 id="infrastructure">Space, power and cooling planned together.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>Buildings A and C are designated for data-center development. Building B supports batteries, utilities and storage, and is excluded from the {site.dataCenterArea.toLocaleString()} sq ft data-center area.</p>
        <p>The existing shared service is {power.service}, supplied by {power.utility} and distributed from Building C. Customer IT allocations follow engineering review and commissioning.</p>
        <p>The B300 systems require new direct liquid cooling. Residual-air cooling is also new, with conventional room cooling and rear-door heat exchangers being compared. A shared plant with separately controlled circuits is one option; each colocation proposal needs its own equipment and service review.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Development milestones</h3>
        <dl class="spec">
          <div><dt>Construction</dt><dd>{site.constructionTarget}<span class="note">{site.contractor} contractor.</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Electrical commissioning</dt><dd>{power.commissioningTarget}<span class="note">Management target.</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Fiber delivery</dt><dd>{network.deliveryTarget}<span class="note">Management target; carrier delivery and acceptance required.</span></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Customer availability follows equipment and facility acceptance. These milestones do not represent live capacity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/power#thermal">Explore power and cooling</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/site">See the campus plan</a></div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="network" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Connectivity</span></p>
    <h2 id="network">High-capacity Dobson fiber is planned.</h2>
    <p>{network.service} connectivity from {network.provider} is planned with a {network.leadTime} delivery estimate. We review tenant bandwidth, traffic patterns and resilience requirements as part of each deployment proposal. The circuit is not yet presented as live service.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="reserve" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">From requirements to proposal</span></p>
    <h2 id="reserve">A clear path to your deployment.</h2>
    <ol class="bullets">
      <li><strong>Share the requirements.</strong> Hardware, IT load, cooling, network, target date and any compliance requirements.</li>
      <li><strong>Review the fit.</strong> We assess the equipment and campus design, and coordinate a site visit where useful.</li>
      <li><strong>Agree the proposal.</strong> The offer defines the allocation, commercial terms, access, support and service commitments before equipment is deployed.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Colocation terms are developed per proposal. Submitting an inquiry starts the review and does not reserve capacity.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Request a deployment review</a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/compute">Explore planned compute</a></div>
  </section>
</Content>
